steam-arm-setup (1.2) stable; urgency=low

  * Launcher frees memory Steam overlay holds in /dev/shm after game
    sessions (two 25 MB buffers per session, kept mapped by web helper).
  * 32-bit titles: -vulkan and -force-vulkan removed (Vulkan forwarding is
    64-bit only); profile key vk32=keep keeps them.
  * Profile key gl32=off: title not detected as 64-bit runs on emulated x86
    Mesa instead of forwarded host Mesa.
  * Start scripts (hl2.sh style) followed to binary they start; 64-bit
    build preferred in arch-switch scripts, crash helpers skipped.
  * Profile args counted by Unity and Godot renderer rules.
  * Source 2 titles logged; component dialog (zenity) with no controlling
    terminal in desktop session. RESEARCH.md added.

 -- Scrumpper <Scrumpper@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000

steam-arm-setup (1.1) stable; urgency=low

  * Check page size before installing anything; stop on 16K or 64K kernel
    with fix for that system. STEAM_ARM_IGNORE_PAGESIZE=1 skips check.
  * New page-size component: on Raspberry Pi, select firmware's 4K page
    kernel in config.txt, keep backup, ask for reboot and second run.
  * New desktop-mode component: menu entry and desktop icon for desktop
    interface. Power menu Switch to Desktop restarts client there.
  * Menu icons from client's own icon in project banner colours; tray
    helper started by launcher.
  * Desktop icons and tray icon are separate components: icon-bigpicture,
    icon-desktop, tray. Installed games, sign-in and settings are kept.
  * Launch handler run by Valve's FEX tool: Steam overlay and MangoHud in
    x86 titles, Godot 4 on OpenGL, title profiles in /etc/steam-arm.
  * Handler engine rules for Unity: Vulkan renderer where player carries
    it, GL 4.5 report otherwise, overlay off for 32-bit players.
  * Direct3D 8 titles under Proton use DXVK (PROTON_DXVK_D3D8=1).
  * Launcher clears shared-memory segments no process maps; after many
    game sessions they filled /dev/shm and every title failed to start.
    Overlay segments steamwebhelper still maps are reclaimed at client
    restart.
  * Installer ships as plain script steam-arm-install.sh; package still
    builds with build-deb.sh.
  * Icons drawn during first start once client has downloaded its icon
    file; KDE menu cache refreshes after.
  * Saved GAMEUSER naming absent account is ignored with warning instead
    of creating that account.
  * Fixed: CPU rendering after fresh install, overlay UI crash, missing
    title bar until next login.

 -- Scrumpper <Scrumpper@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000

steam-arm-setup (1.0) stable; urgency=low

  * Initial release: installer package for Valve's native ARM64 Steam
    client and its supporting components on ARM64 Debian and Ubuntu
    family systems.

